		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=163&amp;p=958#p958"><![CDATA[
I think the name I gave to this is not ideal<br><br>The setting is how much filtering is applied to the DMR signal.<br><br>Eventually I am hoping to be able to support multiple levels of filtering, but at the moment the only filter that can be turned on and off is TS.<br>I <br>I tried to remove CC filtering but I have not managed to get DMR Rx to work when I don’t filter the CC.<br><br>The CC filtering is done in the code, but there are multiple places where the CC is checked and simply changing the code so that the checking could be disabled , in all the places it’s used, caused all sorts of strange problems with the DMR reception.<br><br>TG filtering should also be possible, since the official firmware does this. However I don’t think I would actually use it<br><br>Rather than calling this “DMR mon” , short for DMR Monitor. It should really be called “DMR Filter”, but that takes too many characters on the screen.<br>Perhaps I should change it to   Filter e.g. “Filter:CC,TS,TG”, and on FM show it as “Filter:N/A”<br>Or perhaps “D Filter”<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Nov 27, 2019 8:24 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
